<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n75129" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁρκόω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>make</i> one <i>swear, bind by oath,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Cratin.
				366
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Th.</u>
				276
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				20.26
			</span></i> : folld. by fut.
			inf., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁρκώσαντες πίστεσι μεγάλαις μηδὲν
					μνησικακήσειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					4.74
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ. τινὰ ἦ μὴν ἐμμενεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Is.
					5.33
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ. τινὰς εἴς τινα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Galb.</u>
					10
				</span></i>
			: c. acc. cogn., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ. τοὺς στρατιώτας τοὺς μεγίστους
					ὅρκους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					8.75
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Lys.</u>
				187
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be bound by oath,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Polem.Hist.
				83
			</span></i> ; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁρκίζω.</span>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> abs., <i>administer an
				oath,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
